{"$schema": "https://aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io/api/v1/schemas/ReviewCommentsPage.json", "comments": [{"discussion_id": "01M4RF1YSN57TDG5X075B0WKKM", "discussion_message_count": 0, "id": "01M4RF1YSNRTXM1M5BJ7HEAEBG", "trail_id": "01M3P25ZTS4E5R83CBJ11A9VAS", "repo_id": "01KXJQJRF3YPN2MGMFFDTHZVPK", "review_id": "01M4RF1YSH5J618DMMF6ASPZ1V", "code_version_id": "01M4REF8GHRNJJSWGNTMH4XH86", "actor_id": "agent:trail-review", "actor_display_name": null, "actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "agent:trail-review", "display_name": null, "avatar_url": null, "handles": []}, "body": "`BuildSemanticIndex` calls `index.validate(tree, config.Model)` (line 1010), which forwards to `validateContext(context.Background(), ...)` (line 803) — hardwiring an uncancellable context for the per-row norm check. `validateContext` was explicitly designed to be interruptible: it checks `ctx.Err()` every `semanticScanCheckRows` rows. A user cancellation (SIGINT) that arrives after the last embedding batch cannot abort the validation walk, so for large corpora the process continues for seconds past cancellation. The surrounding comment at line 1017 calls out that `ctx` is checked immediately before the rename, making this the only unchecked window. Replace `index.validate(tree, config.Model)` with `index.validateContext(ctx, tree, config.Model)`.", "severity": "low", "confidence": 0.9, "status": "resolved", "status_reason": "BuildSemanticIndex now passes the caller context to validateContext, including its periodic row checks. All Semantic tests in internal/sem and internal/cli passed (20.5s and 23.3s).", "status_actor_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "status_actor_display_name": "ashtom", "status_actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "display_name": "Thomas Dohmke", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4", "handles": [{"provider": "github", "handle": "ashtom", "is_primary": true}]}, "status_changed_at": "2026-