ashtom", "status_actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "display_name": "Thomas Dohmke", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4", "handles": [{"provider": "github", "handle": "ashtom", "is_primary": true}]}, "status_changed_at": "2026-10-12T14:52:58.338Z", "status_source": "comment_patch", "status_actor_kind": "human", "stale_outcome": "stale", "stale_checked_at": "2026-10-12T14:36:43.880Z", "stale_checked_code_version_id": "01M4R8PRY9QENF86S7WW74GZF6", "client_id": "advsec-20261012-221-squatter", "client_id_hash": "3031bb3a06d8311c18449b6addd245c5f311fe60b330425b379b8968b495b061", "created_at": "2026-10-12T14:31:49.715Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-12T14:52:58.338Z", "location": {"id": "01M4R8DSPNP8AH8NHP2Z4JPEDG", "review_comment_id": "01M4R8DSPND0GSHQF7BPQCDSNX", "code_version_id": "01M4R8D9D9J8QC5P2CVDG9M148", "granularity": "whole_change", "file_path": null, "start_line": null, "start_column": null, "end_line": null, "end_column": null, "selected_text": null, "nearby_text": null, "language": null}}, {"discussion_id": "01M4R8DRE78SR48X94VS2A7AHV", "discussion_message_count": 0, "id": "01M4R8DRE7PXQ7HMHJDGTWDHPS", "trail_id": "01M3P25ZTS4E5R83CBJ11A9VAS", "repo_id": "01KXJQJRF3YPN2MGMFFDTHZVPK", "review_id": "01M4R8DRBRRFV90PFKSV56NFJZ", "code_version_id": "01M4R8D9D9J8QC5P2CVDG9M148", "actor_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "actor_display_name": "ashtom", "actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "display_name": "Thomas Dohmke", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4", "handles": [{"provider": "github", "handle": "ashtom", "is_primary": true}]}, "body": "Partially fixed at 094a9ec4. README.md, AGENTS.md and docs/search.md now distinguish the default no-network analysis from the opt-in loopback embedding channel. Still stale: docs/trust-and-security.md:9-14 (the project security document) says that during analysis the analyzer does not "call hosted APIs, resolve embeddings" and lists the benchmark clone and plugin install as the only networked operations. With ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_* set, index --semantic and query --head make loopback HTTP calls carrying doc comments, signatures and query text. Add the opt-in channel to that Network section. Minor: `query --help` does not list --no-network or say that it disables the channel.", "severity": "low", "confidence": 0.9, "status": "resolved", "status_reason": "The security document now describes the explicit loopback embedding channel, transmitted data, service trust and --no-network behavior. Query help now lists --no-network, and the README semantic anchor is corrected. Help and semantic CLI tests pass.", "status_actor_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "status_actor_display_name": "ashtom", "status_actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "display_name": "Thomas Dohmke", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4", "handles": [{"provider": "github", "handle": "ashtom", "is_primary": true}]}, "status_changed_at": "2026-10-12T15:38:53.404Z", "status_source": "comment_patch", "status_actor_kind": "human", "stale_outcome": "stale", "stale_checked_at": "2026-10-12T14:50:49.770Z", "stale_checked_code_version_id": "01M4R9GK0CA5BMDT5KSC4659Q2", "client_id": "advsec-20261012-221-contract", "client_id_hash": "6501fa79e79f87cd7aa464743bb40e1b6f437c180819b99931b2631d2b421882", "created_at": "2026-10-12T14:31:48.421Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-12T15:38:53.404Z", "location": {"id": "01M4R8DRE71SERM9C29NF7NEMA", "review_comment_id": "01M4R8DRE7PXQ7HMHJDGTWDHPS", "code_version_id": "01M4R8D9D9J8QC5P2CVDG9M148", "granularity": "line", "file_path": "README.md", "start_line": 16, "start_column": null, "end_line": null, "end_column": null, "selected_text": "repository locally with tree-sitter and makes no network requests, model calls,", "nearby_text": null, "language": null}}, {"discussion_id": "01M4R8DQGY748KBDE82HQ1TRQ6", "discussion_message_count": 0, "id": "01M4R8DQGY3MK3N6JH58MB34C9", "trail_id": "01M3P25ZTS4E5R83CBJ11A9VAS", "repo_id": "01KXJQJRF3YPN2MGMFFDTHZVPK", "review_id": "01M4R8DQDEEJDDG9ZYS4SVVGEV", "code_version_id": "01M4R8D9D9J8QC5P2CVDG9M148", "actor_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "actor_display_name": "ashtom", "actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "display_name": "Thomas Dohmke", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4", "handles": [{"provider": "github", "handle": "ashtom", "is_primary": true}]}, "body": "`--no-network` is accepted and silently ignored: `index.go:325` and `search.go:2831` treat it as a no-op and `provider.go:1825` discards `NoNetwork`. With `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_*` set, `index --no-network --semantic` and `query --head --no-network` still POST doc comments (up to 40 lines), signatures, and the query text to the embedding endpoint (verified against a capturing loopback listener). A caller relying on the explicit flag for a no-egress guarantee gets HTTP traffic. Make `--no-network` force the semantic channel off, or reject the combination with `--semantic`.", "severity": "medium", "confidence": 0.95, "status": "resolved", "status_reason": "Query --no-network now disables the configured channel; index --no-network --semantic is rejected before index work. Capturing-loopback regression verifies both formats preserve off:flag, no request is made, and NDJSON still includes search_result record_type. All Semantic and exclusion NDJSON tests pass.", "status_actor_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "status_actor_display_name": "ashtom", "status_actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "01KSAMGR8YW1KR3RF03RC70K93", "display_name": "Thomas Dohmke", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70720?v=4", "handles": [{"provider": "github", "handle": "ashtom", "is_primary": true}]}, "status_changed_at": "2026-10-12T14:53:00.046Z", "status_source": "comment_patch", "status_actor_kind": "human", "stale_outcome": "stale", "stale_checked_at": "2026-10-12T14:50:49.770Z", "stale_checked_code_version_id": "01M4R9GK0CA5BMDT5KSC4659Q2", "client_id": "advsec-20261012-221-nonetwork", "client_id_hash": "f09a3b29e6a269880a49e771242d4681143d0618a50305e2bcf20ae2aecc33d4", "created_at": "2026-10-12T14:31:47.484Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-12T14:53:00.046Z", "location": {"id": "01M4R8DQGYJCQ2AE28QS15ZNKQ", "review_comment_id": "01M4R8DQGY3MK3N6JH58MB34C9", "code_version_id": "01M4R8D9D9J8QC5P2CVDG9M148", "granularity": "line", "file_path": "internal/sem/provider.go", "start_line": 1825, "start_column": null, "end_line": null, "end_column": null, "selected_text": "		includeFiles:     options.IncludeFiles,", "nearby_text": null, "language": null}}, {"discussion_id": "01M4R61W6V8SJB1DQ147EPAYS3", "discussion_message_count": 0, "id": "01M4R61W6VT2HKDARS2E71MY89", "trail_id": "01M3P25ZTS4E5R83CBJ11A9VAS", "repo_id": "01KXJQJRF3YPN2MGMFFDTHZVPK", "review_id": "01M4R61W6QDHWTDJY2YYRY4V17", "code_version_id": "01M4R5BBR8846A83EKQFP0SHJ7", "actor_id": "agent:trail-review", "actor_display_name": null, "actor_identity": {"kind": "account", "account_id": "agent:trail-review", "display_name": null, "avatar_url": null, "handles": []}, "body": "`SemanticScore float64` uses `omitempty`, so a lexical row matched by the semantic channel that happens to have a cosine rounded to exactly `0.0` (i.e. `|cosine| < 0.00005`) will emit the `semantic:embedding` signal but silently omit `semantic_score` from JSON output. Machine consumers that check the signal to expect the field will find it absent, which is an inconsistency in the schema contract. The field is documented as "the channel's cosine for a row it matched, on its own scale", implying it is always present when the signal is. A non-`omitempty` tag (with a dedicated sentinel such as `*float64` or a boolean `has_semantic_score`) or a note in the schema docs would close the gap.", "severity": "low", 