{"baseRefName":"bench/locate-cost","body":"\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-start --\u003e\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/221\n\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-end --\u003e\n\n**DRAFT — do not merge.** An unresolved product decision blocks merge (see below). Stacked on #285 (`bench/locate-cost`, a10582ab).\n\n## What\nAdds an **opt-in** semantic retrieval channel to `entire graph query`. A local embedding model nominates files and symbols, and the results are fused embedding-first with the lexical ranking.\n- **Off by default.** It turns on only when both `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_ENDPOINT` and `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEMANTIC_MODEL` are set. When unconfigured, output is byte-identical to the base across 32 queries × 4 formats × 3 env states.\n- `entire graph index --semantic` builds the index. Queries use it only with `--head` (the committed tree); `--no-semantic` turns it off per call.\n- **Loopback only:** `localhost` or a literal loopback IP. No proxy, no redirects, and names are never resolved by the dialer.\n- **Fails open to lexical** with a `W_SEMANTIC_UNAVAILABLE` warning and a stable code, for a missing index, a timeout, a bad response or a failed nomination snapshot. The reported state is visible in text, agent and JSON output.\n- **Lexical invariance, warm path:** nominations never change lexical scores, IDF or the candidate pool. This is tested against the pre-fusion ranking exactly.\n\n## Evidence: fresh preregistered evaluation (population now spent)\nThe fixture repository had never been used in this work. It has 40 targets (20 documented, 20 not) and model-written realistic queries. The preregistration, three addenda, hashes and the per-query receipts are all written before the arms ran. Gate: channel OFF == pre-feature base on 80/80 queries (rows, spans, ranks, scores, signals).\n\n| realistic, n=40 | found@10 | top3 | rank1 |\n|---|--:|--:|--:|\n| channel off | 22 | 19 | 16 |\n| channel on (`nomic-embed-text`) | **29** | **24** | **19** |\n\n- Paired wins/losses/ties: 7/0/33, exact sign test p = 0.016.\n- Bare-name controls: top3 40/40 in both arms; rank1 21 → 19.\n- **Scorer disclosure:** the verdict depends on a scorer rule fixed before any channel-on output existed. A hit counts if the target overlaps a row's symbol span **or its displayed span**. Under the original symbol-span-only rule the result is 21 → 26, W/L 6/1, and the one loss fails the \"baseline top-3 lost\" clause. That case is a same-file span merge that folds the target into the rank-1 row, whose displayed lines 4–46 include the target (40–46).\n- **Limits:** one repository; model-written queries; retrieval rank only (no token, cost or task claim); warm preindexed path only.\n\n## Review history\nTwo peer reviews (query and safety, Q1–Q5 and F1–F5) and two fresh adversarial re-reviews. Every round found real defects, including defects introduced by earlier fixes. Every finding has a RED→GREEN regression test, and every fix has verified-by-weakening mutation evidence.\n\n## Blocking decisions (human)\n1. **Should the product depend on a local model at all?** This is a trust and resources decision.\n2. Activation/consent: currently env-only.\n3. Model identity: the `:latest` alias is not pinned by digest.\n4. Cold path: nominations evict lexical tail files under `--max-indexed-files`. That is disclosed in `semantic_evicted_files`, but it shifts the surviving BM25 scores slightly.\n5. `semantic_results` now counts rows the channel matched; the JSON format version is not bumped.\n\nRelated: #298 (a `git grep` multi-pattern hang on `main`, found during this evaluation).\n","headRefOid":"652f96751533c23d1366287f1d542974f50e2dd7","isDraft":true,"state":"OPEN","title":"feat(query): opt-in local semantic retrieval channel (draft, needs product decision)"}
